## Planning Tips for Large Groups

### Book in Advance

Walk-ins are always welcome at Infusion Play, but for groups of 10 or more, booking ahead is the smart move. Sessions fill up, and you want your whole team in at the same time. Lock in your date at infusion-play.com.

### Split Into Competing Teams

The Interactive Play rooms are built for competition. Divide your group into teams of three to five, assign team names, and track scores across activities. The points-based reward redemption system gives you a ready-made leaderboard — no extra setup required.

### Mix Activity Formats

Not every employee has the same physical comfort level, and that's fine. Pair laser maze runs with claw machine time to keep the pace balanced and make sure no one gets left behind.

### Use the Downtown Location

546 Yates St sits in the heart of Downtown Victoria, walkable from most offices and hotels in the core. No transport to arrange, no parking to sort out. Show up, play, eat, and head out. When you're coordinating a group, that kind of low-friction setup matters.

